        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>Exit sign in English and French at the CN Tower in Toronto.  The need for this sort of bilingual exit sign was eliminated in 2014, when Ontario adopted the green and white \"running man\" pictogram as the standard for exit signs.\n</p><p>More at <i>The Schumin Web</i>:\n&lt;a href=\"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.schuminweb.com/odds-and-ends/canada-trip-part-1/\">https://www.schuminweb.com/odds-and-ends/canada-trip-part-1/</a>\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"&gt;www.schuminweb.com/odds-and-ends/canada-trip-part-1/&lt;/a&gt;\n</p>\n<i>Ben Schumin is a professional photographer who captures the intricacies of daily life.  This image may be used under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.0.  Please provide artist attribution, as well as a link to the original photo and to the license terms.</i>",
